2 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7732c4e3-3161-5802-ab59-a7cdbdfc5997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559720 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "86cbd155-e168-55e6-b312-a580ef748d0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559773 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559695 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559773 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559773 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559773 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following functions has the domain $(0,2)?$\n\nI. $p:(0,2)\\to \\{0,2\\}$\n\nII. $q:R\\to (0,2)$\n\nIII. $r:(0,2)\\to R$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559773 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559773 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $(0,2),$ the interval from $0$ to $2$ (not including $0$ nor $2$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $(0,2),$ the interval from $0$ to $2$ (not including $0$ nor $2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559780 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559657 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559780 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96828" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559780 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559780 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1b/1b124a0e4439f1b35affa5a38f175a151cbbad88affb12738585da8280bacb23.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559780 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1110805d-d0df-5ae9-af4b-5eeeabf99273" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559780 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X=\\{0,1\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y=\\{0,1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559790 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559790 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96754" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559790 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559790 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of rational numbers.\"*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559790 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "33ee1a61-aa83-56a5-8209-eec63038ff68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559790 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set of rational numbers\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $g:X\\to Q$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $X,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $Q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559794 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559684 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559794 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96819" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559794 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559794 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $g:x↦1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559794 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559794 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $g:x↦1$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $1$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng(x)=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559808 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559808 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559808 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559808 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following functions has the codomain $R?$\n\nI. $p:[0,1]\\to R$\n\nII. $q:R\\to R$\n\nIII. $r:[0,1]\\to [0,1]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559808 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559808 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[0,1],$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559828 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559828 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559828 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559828 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $g$ maps the set of real numbers to the set of rational numbers.\"*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559828 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "915687d1-7d3d-5688-b25a-20c50fc27b30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559828 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence *\"The function $g$ maps the set of real numbers to the set of rational numbers\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $g:R\\to Q$\n\nHere, the domain of $g$ is $R,$ and the codomain of $g$ is $Q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559832 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559832 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104941" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559832 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559832 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $h(x)=2{x}^{3}-3x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559832 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "97bd3e47-4a7d-51fe-87e4-ccb53cfbd7e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559832 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $h(x)=2{x}^{3}-3x$ means that the function $h$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $2{x}^{3}-3x$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nh:x↦2{x}^{3}-3x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559844 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559844 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104951" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559844 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559844 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6a/6ac4933860ceea29b5892d1ea38685dd7d7fbb5e1a6a48cda45b48151b35aeb1.png)\n\nConsider the function $g:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559844 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559844 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $g:X\\to Y$ means that the function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $g$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X=\\{1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$\n\n- the range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559876 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559876 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96757" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559876 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559876 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the interval from $0$ to $3$ inclusive.\"*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559876 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8bbc308-2450-589f-b174-679c413f5f6e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559876 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence *\"The function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the interval from $0$ to $3$ inclusive\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $f:X\\to [0,3]$\n\nHere, the domain of $f$ is $X,$ and the codomain of $f$ is $[0,3].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559883 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559883 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559883 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559883 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following functions has the domain $(-2,0)?$\n\nI. $p:(-2,0)\\to \\{-2,0\\}$\n\nII. $q:(-2,0)\\to (-2,0)$\n\nIII. $r:[-2,0)\\to (0,2)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559883 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559883 #edb/ref 1074 "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $(-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (not including $-2$ nor $0$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $(-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (not including $-2$ nor $0$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $[-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (including $-2$ but not including $0$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559888 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559888 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559888 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559888 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n*\"The function $h$ maps the interval from $0$ to $1$ exclusive to the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $1$ only.\"*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9c7a6ed-7bc4-5fae-bd01-cf7380224c4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559888 #edb/ref 1074 "The sentence *\"The function $h$ maps the interval from $0$ to $1$ exclusive to the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $1$ only\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $h:(0,1)\\to \\{0,1\\}$\n\nHere, the domain of $h$ is $(0,1),$ and the codomain of $h$ is $\\{0,1\\}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
